{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-352710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(3-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(3\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352703" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352703" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity  $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{15}$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u){|}_{-\\pi /3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)-\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(1-0)-\\frac{8}{5}(2+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352491" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352491" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-114304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(2-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352708" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352708" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352867" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352867" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}{csc}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}{tan}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int (\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-74281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$  and  $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-347941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-347941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-347941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-347941" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-347941" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-352798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-352798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\ln(3)}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{-1}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-49277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-362157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-362157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}{|}_{1}^{1/2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-362157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-362157" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-362157" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f391267fbdf8777ae8a478dd8a6bd8d78f66d9604c31eb0ac067758af6a2c3c"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C"] ["math" "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "q-2622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c4e15fd84aa9b9157bd046cd54d7ba3089c8c6a463fe70ed8b65b2d6c7f8cea"} {"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef"} {"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197"}] "usage" {"e-473" [] "e-474" [] "q-49275" [] "q-2622" [] "e-475" []} "basis" 1120 "retractions" [[17592186064775 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\tan^{2} x}{8\\sin^{2} x}dx$."] [17592186064589 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\tan x\\sqrt{\\cos x}dx$."] [17592186064006 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186064006 :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x} = \\csc x\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{1}{\\sin x}(\\cot x + \\sin^{2} x)dx &= \\int(\\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\cot x + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\sin^{2} x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\csc x \\cdot \\cot x + \\sin x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\csc x\\cot xdx + \\int\\sin xdx \\\\\n&=-\\csc x - \\cos x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064007 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186064007 :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x\n$$\n\nto express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/3}\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos^{2} x}dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/3}\\sec x\\tan xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\sec x\\right|_{0}^{π/3} \\\\\n&= \\sec (\\frac{π}{3}) - \\sec (0) \\\\\n&= 2 - 1 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064008 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186064008 :question/worked-solution "We use the identity\n\n$$\n\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}\n$$\n\nand rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}dx &= -\\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ =-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln & \\cos 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}(\\cos 2x)^{-1} & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & \\sec 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186062046 17592186062047 17592186062048 17592186062049 17592186062050 17592186063161 17592186063162 17592186063163 17592186063164 17592186063165] "immutable_fields" [[17592186062045 :answer-field/correct] [17592186062045 :answer-field/id] [17592186062045 :answer-field/key] [17592186062045 :answer-field/type] [17592186063160 :answer-field/correct] [17592186063160 :answer-field/id] [17592186063160 :answer-field/key] [17592186063160 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
